      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T05:57:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m imagining a scenario in the \"hm, I\u0027ll spend three hours of battery on this, but not, like, all of it\" range as a reason someone might want to use the `-t` flag in caffeinate in this mode, which could be exposed by a new command line flag. Which I should probably add to `fetch` if I\u0027m going to go ahead and leave the feature in, but it _is_ definitely on the \"corner case\" side and I could just remove it for simplicity\u0027s sake.\n\nI think the strongest argument for leaving it in (and, to be clear, it is not a strong argument) is that `man caffeinate` is not forthcoming about what happens if you use both `-w` and `-t` together (although it does document that neither flag works if you have caffeinate launch another task), and I did the experiment and I now know the answer. If I remove the logic and someone else wants it later, they have to wonder the same thing and repeat the experiment; if I leave it in, there are no questions about whether it _would_ work! This is probably not a good argument for adding an extraneous feature, so I\u0027ll take it out in the morning. (right now I am just poking at my Mac to see if it kept going with the fetch while the screen was off for a while; it had.)",
      "parentUuid": "bb8fd200_0be27c74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 0
      },
