      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T05:57:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Courtesy of `BooleanOptionalAction`, this is indeed opt-out with the flag `--no-caffeinate`! Note the `default\u003dTrue`. `action\u003dargparse.BooleanOptionalAction` causes `argparse` to create a matched pair of flags, `--caffienate` and `--no-caffeinate`, which act in opposite directions on the same underlying flag value.\n\nAs I understand it, a `--no-` flag usually implies the existence of its antonym as a flag in its own right, so replacing `--no-caffeinate` with this flag/antiflag pair seems like the more \"normal\" approach.",
      "parentUuid": "ebd4d92d_bbb72b3e",
